NAME=rust
VERSION=1.96.0
DESCRIPTION="On-device Rust toolchain — fully-static x86_64-unknown-linux-musl rustc + prebuilt std sysroot + bundled rust-lld (the project's first native Rust code generator)"
CATEGORY=lang
DEPS=musl
URL=https://static.rust-lang.org/dist/rustc-1.96.0-src.tar.xz
SHA256=b99ce16cdf0ecfc761b585ac84d131b46733465a02f8ecd0ff2de9713c62ee09
MAINTAINER=m3os

# Phase 95 — the project's FIRST on-device Rust *compiler* (distinct from Phase
# 94's coreutils, which runs a host-cross-compiled Rust *program*). The Rust
# analog of Phase 85d (on-device Clang/LLVM/LLD): a fully-static
# `x86_64-unknown-linux-musl` `rustc` that compiles + links + runs Rust on m3OS.
#
# Built by `build_rust` (xtask/src/port_build.rs) via the upstream `x.py`
# bootstrap configured for a cross-host static build:
#   build  = x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu   (the stage0 bootstrap runs on the host)
#   host   = x86_64-unknown-linux-musl  (the rustc BINARY is static musl — m3OS's
#                                        custom ld-musl has no real libc.so, so a
#                                        dynamic toolchain can't run; same static
#                                        discipline as clang/python/go)
#   target = x86_64-unknown-linux-musl  (it also generates musl code on-device)
# LLVM is built X86-only (we only target x86_64) with the host clang as the
# musl cross-compiler (the Phase 85d "host clang cross-compiles LLVM" pattern),
# linking a musl libc++. crt-static=true embeds musl into the rustc binary.
#
# The bundled `rust-lld` (rustc's default linker, vendored LLD) is staged INSIDE
# the .m3pkg, so on-device linking needs no external cc/ld and no dependency on
# the (huge, opt-in) clang port. The prebuilt std/core/alloc rlib sysroot is laid
# out relative to the rustc binary (the Phase 85d relocation contract —
# `rustc --print sysroot` resolves under /usr).
#
# DEPS=musl: rustc's OWN source uses proc-macro crates, and a `crt-static` musl
# host cannot build dylibs/proc-macros, so a fully-static rustc is INFEASIBLE.
# rustc is therefore a DYNAMIC musl binary (PT_INTERP=/lib/ld-musl-x86_64.so.1 +
# DT_NEEDED libc.so) that runs on m3OS via the Phase 93 `libc.so` + Rust loader
# (`ports/lib/musl`) — which is exactly why Phase 93 is a Phase 95 dependency. The
# solver installs `/usr/lib/libc.so` first.
#
# The toolchain is a 200–500 MB artifact, so it is OPT-IN behind the
# `M3OS_WITH_RUST` image feature (mirroring `M3OS_WITH_CLANG`); default images
# omit it. `pkg install rust` materializes rustc + the sysroot + rust-lld.
#
# URL note: the pinned `rustc-<ver>-src.tar.xz` from static.rust-lang.org is the
# fully-vendored Rust source (carries Cargo.lock for the `--locked`/vendored
# bootstrap; SHA-256 is the canonical upstream digest), so the heavy host build
# needs no network beyond the stage0 bootstrap compiler x.py auto-downloads.
